WHY THIS SOURCE IS PUBLIC

Seal's central claim is that your meeting audio, transcripts, and notes never
leave your Mac. Every app in this category makes a version of that promise,
and asks you to take it on trust. Publishing the source removes the need to.

You can read exactly what the app does with a recording, confirm that the
only network calls it makes are the update check, the first-run model
download, and licence activation, and check that none of them carry meeting
content. That is the whole reason this repository is open to read.

Seal is not open-source software. This is a source-available licence: the
code is published for inspection and personal use, not for redistribution.
The terms below are what govern; this section is only here to explain them.


